  "body": "I try to find way for increase size limit of `_get_joined_profile_from_event_id` cache in Synapse 1.22.1.\r\nWith default setup via Prometheus stats I see that it is limited to 5K items, so I fill those params in `conf.d/caching.yml` file:\r\n```\r\nevent_cache_size: 900K\r\n\r\ncaches:\r\n   #global_factor: 1.5\r\n   global_factor: 4.0\r\n   per_cache_factors:\r\n     _get_joined_profile_from_event_id: 50.0\r\n```\r\nand restart Synapse, but see that the limit is not changed, here is the chart with restart event at ~11:05:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/336662/98927020-113b2200-24e9-11eb-8a78-d579a351446e.png)\r\n\r\nWhy increasing `per_cache_factors` doesn't increase 5K limit - is this a Synapse issue, or I must configure this limit in some other place?",
